4. Hypotheses

H1 — Conditional divergence. \Delta V(P \mid f) exhibits a threshold f^* at which |\Delta V| exceeds \delta_{\min}. Classification: aligned if \Delta V > \delta_{\min} beyond f^*, independent if |\Delta V| \le \delta_{\min}, conflicting if \Delta V < -\delta_{\min}. Classification is claimed only if stable across the multiverse and across the interquartile range of unanchored-operational parameters.

H2 — Structure beats mass, out of sample. Graph indicators including \delta_R and \bar{\beta} predict function-level failure more accurately than three baselines (imported mass ratio, imported cost ratio, count of imported components), with a strong fourth baseline (betweenness centrality plus lead-time-weighted exposure) included to prevent a strawman comparison. Cross-validation on held-out configurations and disruptions, margin \Delta\text{AUC} \ge 0.05 (a pre-registered convention), reported under all three recipe-set variants.

H3 — Marginal cost of resilience. The Pareto frontier between V_{\text{net}} and structural resilience has an identifiable knee. Disproportionate is defined as marginal cost above a registered multiple \theta_{\text{knee}} of average cost. Knee via Kneedle and sensitivity-knee (snee) with bootstrap intervals. If the 95% CI width exceeds a pre-registered fraction of the frontier range, the knee is declared unidentifiable—an informative result.

H0 — Data adequacy (gate). The retrodiction discriminability test (§5.2) is passed: the candidate data reconstruct a graph and model that reproduce the direction and approximate magnitude of at least two documented propagation effects within a pre-registered tolerance interval \tau_{\text{retro}}. If H0 fails, the audit returns NO-GO and no confirmatory claim about H1–H3 is made.

