Appendix F — Latin hypercube design and discrete rounding

F.1 Continuous LHS

For n samples in p=3 dimensions, the LHS construction is:

1. Partition each dimension into n equiprobable strata I_{i,k} = [(k-1)/n, k/n), k = 1,\dots,n.
2. For each dimension i, draw u_{i,k} \sim \mathcal{U}(I_{i,k}) independently.
3. Apply an independent uniform random permutation \sigma_i to the strata indices of dimension i.
4. The j-th sample is (u_{1,\sigma_1(j)}, u_{2,\sigma_2(j)}, u_{3,\sigma_3(j)}).

Stratification guarantee. In each one-dimensional margin, exactly one point falls in each stratum. The permutations ensure that the joint distribution is not degenerate; the estimator of any additive function has variance at most that of plain Monte Carlo up to a lower-order correction.

F.2 Scaling to physical bounds

f = f_{\min} + u_1 (f_{\max} - f_{\min}), \qquad
d = \operatorname{round}\bigl(d_{\min} + u_2 (d_{\max} - d_{\min})\bigr), \qquad
k = \operatorname{round}\bigl(k_{\min} + u_3 (k_{\max} - k_{\min})\bigr).

F.3 Discrete-rounding correction

Rounding destroys one-dimensional stratification when the integer range is smaller than n. The correction adopted is stratified integer sampling with replacement:

· Let n_d = d_{\max} - d_{\min} + 1 and n_k = k_{\max} - k_{\min} + 1.
· Partition the index set \{0,\dots,n-1\} into n_d (resp. n_k) blocks of approximately equal size, and draw an integer from the corresponding block.
· This guarantees marginal uniformity over the discrete support to within \lceil n/n_d \rceil sampling error, which is reported in the sampler diagnostics.

The correction matters because uncorrected rounding can systematically under-sample the extreme integer values (e.g., d = d_{\max}), biasing the estimate of the tail of the disruption distribution and hence of \Delta V at large f.

F.4 Crossing with the configuration space

The full factorial 3^{4} = 81 is crossed with the n disruption samples, yielding 81 n simulation cells per recipe-set variant. For n = 50 and three recipe variants, the confirmatory execution matrix is 81 \times 50 \times 3 = 12{,}150 runs before multiverse axes other than recipe-set are crossed. Runtime estimates are reported in the stage plan (01C).

