Appendix J — Variance decomposition model

J.1 Model

For configuration c and disruption d:

Y_{c,d} = \mu + \beta_I I_c + \boldsymbol{\beta}_G \mathbf{g}_c + \beta_R R_c + \beta_X (I_c R_c) + \boldsymbol{\beta}_Y (\mathbf{g}_c R_c) + u_c + \varepsilon_{c,d},

with u_c \sim \mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_u^2) and \varepsilon_{c,d} \sim \mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_\varepsilon^2) independent.

J.2 Variance shares

\text{Share}_{\text{inventory}} = \frac{\operatorname{Var}(\beta_I I + \beta_X I R)}{\operatorname{Var}(Y)},
\quad
\text{Share}_{\text{structure}} = \frac{\operatorname{Var}(\boldsymbol{\beta}_G \mathbf{g} + \boldsymbol{\beta}_Y \mathbf{g} R)}{\operatorname{Var}(Y)},

\text{Share}_{\text{reconfiguration}} = \frac{\operatorname{Var}(\beta_R R)}{\operatorname{Var}(Y)},
\quad
\text{Share}_{\text{config}} = \frac{\sigma_u^2}{\operatorname{Var}(Y)},
\quad
\text{Share}_{\text{residual}} = \frac{\sigma_\varepsilon^2}{\operatorname{Var}(Y)}.

The variance of an interaction term is computed by the delta method or by parametric bootstrap; the two are compared.

J.3 Interaction-first reporting rule

Interactions I_c R_c and \mathbf{g}_c R_c are estimated and reported before the main-component shares. A large interaction share means the three-way decomposition is not additive, and the interpretation of the "reconfiguration" component as a separable contribution is not licensed. In that case the multiverse reports the decomposition as interaction-dependent and the main-component shares are demoted to descriptive indicators.

J.4 Stability across the multiverse

The variance shares are recomputed in each multiverse cell. The stability of the ranking (inventory vs structure vs reconfiguration) across cells is reported as a fraction. If the ranking flips across cells, that instability is the finding.

